Z||000009||kslish||10-15-2001||01:12 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mark:<BR><B>Ken,<P>What is the starting location and time for the fall cruise to Fiero Warehouse?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am not coordinating this event for the club, but here is the e-mail I recieved on it:<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Hi everybody,<P>   Here are the final details of the cruise for this year. In order to save time and postage, people with e-mail will get an e-mail, and everybody else will get a flier. The fliers are copies of this letter.<P>   First, the address for Elby's Big Boy restaraunt is 1370 West Chestnut St., Washington, Pa. Take I 70 W to The US-40 exit(exit#4), towards Chestnut St. Keep right at the fork in the ramp. Merge onto US-40. I've never been there, I hope there are signs. I'm going to try to be there around 9:30 AM, and will try to find this place. We need to get on the road by 11:00, so we can arrive at Doug's place by 12:00.<P>   If anybody would like to come but can't make breakfast, the directions to Doug's place are- Take I 70 W to Wheeling, then follow I 470 W to Rt 2 south. Take the 3rd exit on Rt 2 south (South Marshall St). Turn left at the bottom of the ramp, then go approx. 1 mile. The Fiero warehouse is on the right, next to the fire station. <P>   Hope a bunch of you can make it, Doug has some parts pick-ups arranged, and some of the Ohio fiero people may show up, this sounds like this could be an interesting day. Doug volunteered to do a demo on installing GT quarter windows, and a friend of his may be there to show us a few things about fiberglass. <P>   Got to go, see you there-  Rick (ricks86@wpia.net)<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hope this helps, <BR>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
